.TH BYTEKEYSD 8 "October 2026" "ByteKeys 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bytekeysd \- ByteKeys keyboard lighting service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bytekeysd
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bytekeysd
owns the keyboard lighting hardware. It applies the chosen lighting, runs
effects and automation rules, restores everything at boot and after
suspend, and serves the
.BR bytekeys (1)
tools over a Unix socket. Anyone may query it; changes are accepted from
root, members of the
.B bytekeys
group and the user of the active local session.
.PP
It is normally started by systemd
.RB ( bytekeysd.service ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Control socket (default /run/bytekeys/bytekeysd.sock).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Where settings are kept (default /var/lib/bytekeys).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-input
Do not watch input devices. Disables idle rules and the Reactive effect.
Only the time of the last input is ever used, never which keys were pressed.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Add simulated keyboards.
.TP
.B \-v
Debug logging.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bytekeys (1),
.BR bytekeys-gui (1)
